// UNSOUNDNESS repro (U3a): a temporal leaf with a FREE variable shared
// between a restrictor conjunct and a filter, with no `exists` binder. The
// conjunct-order check models safe-range semantics (the `formerly` restricts
// `a`, then `a > 100` filters), but the top-level boolean evaluator does not
// implement that semantics: bindings from a non-bare-predicate left conjunct
// are discarded, so the accepted policy evaluates to FALSE on every trace —
// including one containing a 150-amount transfer. A `when` guard that never
// fires; on a `forbid`, fail-open.
//
// Expected: rejected at parse-time binding checks — temporal leaves must be
// closed; wrap the variable: `exists (a: Long). (…)`.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Read", resource)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.amount: a }
    && a > 100
};
